; alasql lists react-native-fs as an optionalDependency, and that package peer-depends
; on react-native and react-native-windows. npm auto-installs peers, so the whole React
; Native / metro toolchain landed in the production tree and `npm audit --omit=dev`
; reported seven high-severity advisories for code the bundle never imports (issue #115).
; Turning off peer auto-install drops the toolchain and leaves react-native-fs itself,
; whose own dependencies are just utf8 and base-64. Optional deps still install, which
; matters because esbuild ships its platform binaries as optionalDependencies.
legacy-peer-deps=true
